bevy-horizon: NVK's timestampPeriod on the Switch

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at d4a00ea0ab3f59afb967cc5d779e4263d237bd77, after 0001. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this
text before the first "diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

NVK reports timestampPeriod = 1.0 (with a FIXME), right for desktop GPUs whose PTIMER counts
nanoseconds. The Tegra X1's PTIMER (GM20B) is designed for a 31.25 MHz reference, adding 32 per
tick so the count is in ns, but it is clocked from 19.2 MHz: nvgpu's include/nvgpu/ptimer.h
(PTIMER_REF_FREQ_HZ = 31250000, "a period of 32 nanoseconds"; MIT) and the gm20b platform data
(ptimer_src_freq = 19200000, platform_gk20a_tegra.c; GPL-2.0, only the number). So one count is 31.25 / 19.2 = 1.6276 ns,
and GPU times read with timestampPeriod 1.0 (wgpu's timestamp queries, Bevy's
RenderDiagnosticsPlugin) come out 1.63 times too short. UnleashedRecomp-NX measured the same
factor (1.627) on hardware.

vkGetCalibratedTimestampsKHR's device timestamps (nvkmd_switch_dev_get_gpu_timestamp, libnx
nvGpuGetTimestamp) are raw PTIMER counts too, so they stay in step with the GPU's own.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
index a9a7985..a6821b4 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
@@ -994,8 +994,16 @@ nvk_get_device_properties(const struct nvk_instance *instance,
       .storageImageSampleCounts = sample_counts,
       .maxSampleMaskWords = 1,
       .timestampComputeAndGraphics = true,
+#ifdef __SWITCH__
+      /* The Tegra X1's PTIMER counts in units of 1 ns of a 31.25 MHz reference
+       * (32 per tick) but is clocked from 19.2 MHz, so one unit is
+       * 31.25 / 19.2 = 1.6276 ns (nvgpu: PTIMER_REF_FREQ_HZ, ptimer_src_freq).
+       */
+      .timestampPeriod = 31250000.0f / 19200000.0f,
+#else
       /* FIXME: Is timestamp period actually 1? */
       .timestampPeriod = 1.0f,
+#endif
       .maxClipDistances = 8,
       .maxCullDistances = 8,
       .maxCombinedClipAndCullDistances = 8,
